u know  it's it is indeed a a bet on gas but in  that sense the company is a very very  important guest company as well so we  are about at this point in time she'll  stand alone  fifty/fifty company when it comes to gas  and oil and really combining it with wit  BG will not change that ratio  fundamentally so yes indeed it will be a  much enhanced integrated gas company but  we see gas also is a very very important  fuel for the future bear in mind this is  a fuel that does 50 percent less carbon  dioxide emissions than coal in power  generation and we therefore see gets to  be very very important bricks or even a  destination fuel for many decades to  come so we think a bet on gas is a good  thing is this signed sealed delivered do  you see any big hurdles going forward to  get this deal through well there will be  has been any deal of this magnitude will  of course be approvals that we will have  to go through so the key approvals that  we have identified are of course Brazil  because that's a very large portfolio  Australia China and of course we will  have to go to Brussels as well I think  the key ones are going to be the these  four probably but Brussels being the  least complex one because the the  overlap is is or the complementarity is  easiest in Europe it will take time  Jonathan but we are confident if people  get through this otherwise you would not  have embarked on it it will take us  probably until early quarter one next  year before we can complete but I just  want to talk about the price paid very  quickly as well 47 billion pounds do I  look at that or do I look at the premium  if I look at the premium it kind of  looks a little bit expensive a 50  percent premium I was looking at some of  the deals through the Bloomberg dates or  anything over ten billion dollars  typically in this sector carries a 40  percent premium what was the thinking in  the price paid well you have to really  look at this on the basis of of a net  asset value place so you look at the NPV  of the assets how it's being valued at  this point in time what that NPV would  be worth or rather what these assets  would be worth if there were combined  with ours that's the way you typically  do this on Lachi and P deals now this is  a super large C and P deal but if you  look at it this way you look at what  this asset set is worth for the combined  company and how it's being valued in the  market  there is a huge gap in valuation are  some of that you have to give of course  to shareholders in the form of the  control premium but the premium really  is resultant again if you look in the  sector a premium of 50 percent this  pretty much sort of middle of the road  but if you look again at what it does  for the sort of key metrics of the  company you will see it is immediately  going to be a creative in terms of  operating cash per share earnings per  share is going to be accreta from 17  onwards significantly a creative from 18  onwards and in terms of free cash flow  is going to be very seriously a creative  almost immediately as well and that of  course is driving the logic of the deal  together with the fact that we'll use  this as a springboard to divest  significant parts of their large group  to make it a much more focused company  and return that to shareholders as well  yeah you talk about earnings per share  of course that might be flooded somewhat  by that 25 billion dollar buyback  between 2017 and 2020 what is the  thinking behind that buyback well the  thinking is as follows we want to have  not only the sort of basic logic of  putting two portfolios together and then  really work the value out of it by the  capability of shell we want to have also  this deal as a springboard for making  the company much more focused much more  simple much more straightforward so what  we aim to build is a company that has  three core pillars a very very strong  world-class deep water business a very  very strong world-class integrated gas  energy business and then some very very  strong cash engines as well it's being  able to do up to twenty billion dollars  of cash per annum by the end of the  decade and then there's some long term  options now what we're going to do is is  significantly streamlined therefore the  existing portfolio and we think that  about 30 billion dollars worth of assets  will be sold in a process in the 16 to  18 period that's  together with the increased operating  cash together with a much disciplined  approach to capex will basically make a  lot of free cash flow available that we  return back to  holder's first of all by diffident then  you know a dividend policy but on top of  it a very significant buyback 25 billion  dollars which will offset part of the  script or dump out the entire script but  on top of it we'll also start paying  back the equity issue that people have  to do to complete this deal Ben I'm very  sorry but we have literally 30 seconds  left so this won't have to be a quick  one you buy BG we are looking at anyone  else when you were looking at making  this deal the likes of BP for instance  are we've been looking at of course a  range of companies for a long time but  this by far is the most compelling deal  because think of not just for us for the  industry Ben Vandiver and great to have  you join us this morning Ben van Beurden  the CEO of Royal Dutch Shell

